{{define "research"}}
<section class="o-hero-page research-hero hard-purpose-hero">
<div class="research-hero-copy">
<p class="o-hero-page-eyebrow">@@HARD_STATUS@@</p>
<h1 class="o-hero-page-title">@@HARD_TITLE@@</h1>
<p class="t-body-s u-mt-3">@@HARD_FULL_NAME@@</p>
<p class="o-hero-page-lede">A polished result can still be unfinished.</p>
<p class="t-body-m u-mt-4">AI can produce a convincing screen before the work behind it has been thought through. This protocol helps people inspect the missing structure before committing to the next build.</p>
<div class="m-cta-pair u-mt-5"><a class="button button-primary" data-primary-task href="#start">Review one workflow</a><a class="button button-secondary" data-primary-task id="agent-tools" href="/research/ai-readiness/developers">Developer Library</a></div>
<p class="t-body-s u-mt-4">Start with the questions below. The Developer Library holds all 15 criteria, MCP, Skill and optional Jev setup.</p>
</div>
<figure class="o-card-archetype hard-surface-example" aria-labelledby="surface-example-caption">
<div class="hard-example-window" aria-hidden="true">
<div class="cluster cluster-2"><span class="tag tag-mono">DEMO / BOOKING</span><span class="hard-example-dot"></span></div>
<p class="t-title-l u-mt-5">Your next conversation,<br>one click away.</p>
<p class="t-body-s u-mt-3">Choose a consultation time.</p>
<div class="hard-example-slots"><span>9:00 AM</span><span>11:00 AM</span><span>2:00 PM</span></div>
<div class="hard-example-confirm">Confirm booking</div>
</div>
<figcaption id="surface-example-caption"><p class="t-eyebrow">Looks finished. Still unanswered.</p><p class="t-body-m">What if payment succeeds, but the booking does not?</p><p class="t-body-s">Constructed illustration, not an interactive service or a pilot result.</p></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>

<section class="o-section o-section--bordered" id="scenarios"><div class="o-section-inner stack stack-5">
<div class="hard-section-intro"><p class="t-eyebrow">01 / Make the hidden work visible</p><h2 class="t-title-xl">Review the structure, not just the surface.</h2><p class="t-body-l">Take the same booking example out of its polished screen. The happy path is easy to draw. Recovery is where the unanswered decisions appear.</p></div>
<figure class="o-card-archetype hard-structure-example" aria-labelledby="structure-caption">
<ol class="hard-flow t-body-m" aria-label="Proposed booking flow"><li><span class="tag tag-mono">1</span><strong>Choose a time</strong><span class="t-body-s">What if it is no longer available?</span></li><li><span class="tag tag-mono">2</span><strong>Take payment</strong><span class="t-body-s">What prevents a duplicate charge?</span></li><li><span class="tag tag-mono">3</span><strong>Create booking</strong><span class="t-body-s">What if this step fails?</span></li></ol>
<div class="m-callout hard-open-question"><div class="m-callout-body"><p class="t-title-m">Payment taken. No booking. Now what?</p><p class="t-body-m">The recovery path, stored data, refund authority and support owner are not defined in this example. Better typography cannot answer those questions.</p></div></div>
<figcaption class="t-body-s" id="structure-caption">The simplified view exposes questions; it does not prove a defect, create missing evidence or pass a gate. Check each concern against a requirement and the actual artifact.</figcaption>
</figure>
<details class="hard-detail"><summary class="t-title-m">Why this research started</summary><p class="t-body-m">The author's starting observation came from architectural previsualization: an architect described using a watercolor treatment on an intermediate 3D view so clients would discuss the overall structure rather than treat a polished rendering as a finished design. This is an origin anecdote, not evidence of a measured effect.</p><p class="t-body-m">AI-assisted work raises a related question: if the first artifact already looks finished, when do people inspect the decisions underneath? The proposed study tests visual fidelity and defect detection while keeping content, behavior and defects constant. It does not establish that all AI-built work skips design steps.</p><p class="t-body-m">For practical review, preserve the original artifact and create a separate view of its structure. Do not blur labels or remove information people need. A wireframe or diagram helps only if it makes the relevant work inspectable.</p><a class="link" href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-2/research-boundary.html">Research question and limits</a></details>
</div></section>

<section class="o-section o-section--bordered" id="criteria"><div class="o-section-inner stack stack-5">
<div class="hard-section-intro"><p class="t-eyebrow">02 / Look across the layers</p><h2 class="t-title-xl">The missing piece may not be visual.</h2><p class="t-body-m">Start with a real need and the work people do today. Then inspect these four views together. They organize the conversation; they are not four new scores or a replacement for the six gates.</p></div>
<div class="o-persona-grid research-role-grid">
<article class="o-persona-card"><div class="o-persona-card-summary"><div class="o-persona-card-head"><span class="m-avatar" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3 class="o-persona-card-name">Experience and information</h3><p class="o-persona-card-role">Can people understand the task?</p></div></div><p class="o-persona-card-jtbd">Inspect the hierarchy, labels, choice load, repeated actions and alignment with the user's actual goal. Judge these against a task, not personal taste.</p></div></article>
<article class="o-persona-card"><div class="o-persona-card-summary"><div class="o-persona-card-head"><span class="m-avatar" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3 class="o-persona-card-name">Workflow and architecture</h3><p class="o-persona-card-role">Do the parts fit together?</p></div></div><p class="o-persona-card-jtbd">Map states, transitions, dependencies and handoffs. Show where work starts, ends, fails and recovers, including who may act.</p></div></article>
<article class="o-persona-card"><div class="o-persona-card-summary"><div class="o-persona-card-head"><span class="m-avatar" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3 class="o-persona-card-name">Implementation and evidence</h3><p class="o-persona-card-role">What has actually been demonstrated?</p></div></div><p class="o-persona-card-jtbd">Connect requirements to the exact artifact and its checks. Separate simulated behavior, implemented behavior and untested assumptions.</p></div></article>
<article class="o-persona-card"><div class="o-persona-card-summary"><div class="o-persona-card-head"><span class="m-avatar" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div><h3 class="o-persona-card-name">People and operation</h3><p class="o-persona-card-role">Who carries the remaining work?</p></div></div><p class="o-persona-card-jtbd">Name review, correction, escalation, support and ownership. Keep projected savings separate from actual performance in use.</p></div></article>
</div>
<!-- CRITERIA -->
<p class="t-body-s">The intended benefit is a next step the team can explain, with fewer unresolved assumptions hidden by appearance. Whether the protocol improves real decisions remains to be tested.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="o-section o-section--bordered" id="start"><div class="o-section-inner stack stack-5">
<div class="hard-section-intro"><p class="t-eyebrow">03 / Start small</p><h2 class="t-title-xl">One workflow. One review. One next action.</h2><p class="t-body-l">Bring a recent case of today's work, the proposed artifact and someone who knows the work. An advisor can ask the questions and take notes. No installation is needed.</p></div>
<div id="quick-six"><ol class="research-steps hard-six t-body-m">
<li><strong>What happens today?</strong><p>Show the people, steps, time, failures and rework in a recent case. Missing baseline means stop; ROI stays indeterminate.</p></li>
<li><strong>What needs to improve, for whom?</strong><p>Name an actual need and a result you can check, including people affected by the workflow.</p></li>
<li><strong>How does it work, including failure?</strong><p>Use a structure view to inspect information, choices, states, recovery and human or agent authority.</p></li>
<li><strong>What demonstrates the behavior?</strong><p>Connect each important requirement to an exact artifact revision and a relevant test or validation.</p></li>
<li><strong>What work remains for people?</strong><p>Count checking, correction, escalation and manual work before claiming savings.</p></li>
<li><strong>What next step does the evidence support?</strong><p>Apply the risk depth and record the recommendation, owner, resource limit and reason to revisit it.</p></li>
</ol></div>
<p class="t-body-m">Check risk first. QUICK-6 is for low-risk work with records available. Moderate, high or unknown risk needs the full profile. A failed or missing gate stops the short review; it cannot be averaged away. The 15-minute target remains untested.</p>
<div class="m-cta-pair" id="downloads"><a class="button button-primary" data-primary-task href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-2/HARD-QUICK-6-0.2-preview.2.pdf" download>Download QUICK-6</a><a class="button button-secondary" data-primary-task href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-2/PROTOCOL.html">Read the full protocol</a></div>
<details class="hard-detail"><summary class="t-title-m">Other documents and downloads</summary><div class="stack stack-3 t-body-m">
<a class="link" href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-2/HARD-Protocol-0.2-preview.2.pdf" download>Download protocol PDF</a>
<a class="link" href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-2/WORKSHEET.html">Conversation worksheet</a>
<a class="link" href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-2/HARD-Full-Profile-0.2-preview.2.pdf">Full risk-tiered profile PDF</a>
<a class="link" href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-2/HARD-External-Pilot-Packet-0.2-preview.2.pdf">External pilot packet PDF</a>
<a class="link" href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-2/HARD-Protocol-0.2-preview.2.zip">Source package</a>
